# Vault writing

## Wikilinks

- Link a concept **once per page**, on the first useful mention.
- Later repeats stay plain text (same page, same note target).
- Do not link every occurrence of Lumenhold, Stonewake, Blackstone, etc. in a paragraph.
- If two display words point at the same note in one sentence (e.g. Blackstone and Illumination), link only one.
- **Exceptions**: intentional nav/rosters (Quick links, hubs, Bases). Those may list many links.

```markdown
<!-- good -->
Journey to [[Lumenhold]] for [[Stonewake Festival]]. Have you been to Lumenhold before?

<!-- bad -->
Journey to [[Lumenhold]] for [[Stonewake Festival]]. Have you been to [[Lumenhold]] or the [[Stonewake Festival|Festival]] before?
```

## Prose

- Prefer short, concrete sentences. No em dashes.
- Avoid purple / AI-sounding filler. Keep lore notes basic unless expanding on purpose.
- Placeholders stay obvious (`[[IDK YET WORLD]]`, `[[NAME OF …]]`).

## Frontmatter

- Allowed keys: `aliases`, `tags`, `publish`, `faction` (gods only), `title` (home only).
- Tags: singular Title Case kinds — see `.cursor/skills/vault-tags/taxonomy.md`.
- `publish: true` for player-facing lore; `false` for Void gods and private PC material.
- Do not put Light/Void/Neutral in tags when `faction:` is set.

## Structure

- One idea per note when it will grow; combine only when terms are the same system (e.g. Illumination + Blackstone).
- Folders: `Locations/`, `Events/`, `Lore/`, `People/Gods/`, `Factions/`, `People/PCs/`.
